    <string name="faq_use_title">How to use MyMoneyTree</string>
    <string name="faq_use_body">Log in, then use Home for a snapshot of your money, Transactions for every income and expense, Categories to group spending, and Analysis to review totals over time.</string>
    <string name="faq_cost_title">How much does it cost for MyMoneyTree?</string>
    <string name="faq_cost_body">MyMoneyTree is free to use. Your budget data is stored on this device.</string>
    <string name="faq_contact_title">How to contact support?</string>
    <string name="faq_contact_body">Open Help and switch to Contact Us. You can email customer service or visit the website and social links listed there.</string>
    <string name="faq_password_title">How can I reset my password if I forget it?</string>
    <string name="faq_password_body">On the Log In screen, tap Forgot Password, enter your email, then use the security pin to choose a new password.</string>
    <string name="faq_privacy_title">Are there any privacy or data security measures in place?</string>
    <string name="faq_privacy_body">Your account, transactions, and receipts stay in the local MyMoneyTree database on this phone. We do not upload your budget to a server.</string>
    <string name="faq_settings_title">Can I customize settings within the application?</string>
    <string name="faq_settings_body">Yes. Open Profile, then Edit Profile to change your name, phone, email, photo, and notification preference.</string>
    <string name="faq_delete_title">How can I delete my account?</string>
    <string name="faq_delete_body">Account deletion is not in the app yet. Use Contact Us to reach customer service if you need help removing your data.</string>
    <string name="faq_history_title">How do I access my expense history?</string>
    <string name="faq_history_body">Open the Transactions tab for the full list, or open a category in Category Garden to see expenses for that group.</string>
    <string name="faq_offline_title">Can I use the app offline?</string>
    <string name="faq_offline_body">Yes. MyMoneyTree keeps your budget on the device, so Home, transactions, and categories work without an internet connection.</string>
